Graph: A non-linear data structure used to represent relationship
between objects.

ex: Social network, Google maps, Computer Network, Flight routes

A graph consists of :
 i)Vertices(nodes) -> Objects
 ii)Edges -> connection between the objects
 
 
 Vertex: individual element in a graph
 Edge: Connection between two vertices
 Adjacent vertices: Vertices that are directly connected by an edge.
 Degree: Number of edges connected to a vertes.
 
 Degree(3)=3
 Degree(2)=3
 
 Types of graphs:
 i)Undirected graph: Edges have no direction.
 ii)Directed graph: Edges have direction.
 iii)Weighted graph: Each edge has a weight/cost.
 iv)Unweighted graph: No weight.
 v)Cyclic graph: contains cycles.
 vi)Acyclic graph: No cycle.
 vii)Connected graph: Every vertex is reachable from every other vertex.
 viii)Disconnect  graph: Some vertices are not reachable.
 
 
 
 
 Graph representation:
 
 i)Adjacency matrix
 ii)Adjacency list
 
 1 -> if edge exist 
 0 -> if doesn't exist
 
 Undeirected graph
   A B C D E
 A 0 1 1 0 0
 B 1 0 0 1 1
 C 1 0 0 1 0
 D 0 1 1 0 1
 E 0 1 0 1 0
 
 1 -> if edge exist 
 0 -> if doesn't exist
 
 
 directed graph
   A B C D E
 A 0 1 1 0 0
 B 0 0 0 0 1
 C 0 0 0 0 0
 D 0 1 1 0 1
 E 0 0 0 0 0
 
 
 
 Adjacency List:
 Array of list 
 vertex  Neighbours
 A ->    B ->  C 
 B ->    A ->  D ->   E
 C ->    A    D
 D ->    C    B   E
 E ->    B    D
 
 
 
 Traversal:
 i)DFS(Depth First Search)
 DFS explores as far as possible along a branch `before backtracking.
   Go deep first, then comeback.
   
  Stack(Or recursion) 
   
 ii)BFS(Breadth First search)
 BFS explores level by level.
 
   Visit all neighbors first before going deeper.
   
   Queue
   
Cycle detection in a graph:

A cycle exist if we can start from a vertex and return to the 
same vertex by following graph edges.

In undirected graph:
i)DFS + parent tracking
ii)BFS + parent tracking

Condition: If neighbor is already visited and is not parent -> cycle exist


   
   Given an adjacency list adj[][] representaing an undirected
   graph, determine whether the graph contains a cycle/loop or
   not.
   
   adj[][]=[[1,2],[0,2],[0,1,3],[2]]
   
   vertices=0,1,2,3
   
   
   
  In directed graph: 
  i)DFS + recursion stack
  ii)Topological sorting(Kanh's Algo)
 
 
 
 Topological sorting: It is a linera ordering of vertices 
 such that for every directed edge  u->v, vertex u comes 
 before v in ordering.
 
 
